  "recipeDetail": "Comments from the Creator\nThe \"Crisp Teal Contrast\" look infuses the image with sharp, dramatic contrasts, enhancing both shadows and highlights. Cool tones dominate, with a slight bluish tint giving the scene a fresh, edgy feel. Colors retain their richness without being overly saturated, while skin tones stay natural with a cooler undertone. Shadows are deep, adding a bold sense of depth and structure. This look brings intensity and clarity, perfect for portraiture where depth and mood are essential.\n\nWhen using this recipe, we recommend setting [Active D-Lighting] to [Extra high] or [Extra high 1] on your camera. Selecting either of these options preserves details in highlights while achieving rich, cinema-like tonal gradations in your image.",
